## Tracked findings (when this repository has audits or reviews)

- Keep stable finding IDs and one current remediation ledger in the finding document. The ledger is
  current status authority; progress files are chronological evidence, not current status.
- Explicit states help handoffs: `OPEN`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `CODE_COMPLETE`, `PRODUCTION_PENDING`,
  `CLOSED`, `BLOCKED_DECISION`, `ACCEPTED_RISK`, `SUPERSEDED`. `CODE_COMPLETE` and
  `PRODUCTION_PENDING` are not `CLOSED`; closure requires every applicable acceptance test and
  live/external exit gate.
- Check the ledger and current implementation before starting, update both with the remediation,
  and reopen closed work only with contradictory evidence.
- Accepted risks need an owner, decision date, compensating controls, and review/expiry date.
- Optional: if this repo keeps a durable plan, use one live plan file plus one lifecycle archive.
  Tracked sections need a stable ID and an exit gate; shipped means that gate has evidence.

